   161	
   162	For a file that is hard-protected except for a very small set of declaration
   163	keys, use `fileRules[].protectedExceptAnchors`. This is an inverse allowlist:
   164	every hunk is an unacknowledgeable `protected_anchor` violation unless **all**
   165	of its parsed declaration anchors appear in the listed exception array. A hunk
   166	with no parseable anchor fails closed, rather than being treated as an allowed
   167	exception. `scope_contract_acknowledge` cannot downgrade these violations in any
   168	mode, including `shadow`.
